From: Ryan Stoffel <stoffel.thomas.ryan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 07:42:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] strip: open a regular window instead of the Agents window

The Agents window is upstream's separate agent workbench. It opens when a
window loads the agent sessions workspace, and every way to open it goes
through ensureAgentsWindow: the --agents flag, agent session links, a
second instance started with --agents, and the in-app command. wisp's
coordinator replaces it.

Upstream's AI switch hides the in-app buttons, but not the others. With
chat.disableAIFeatures on, `wisp --agents` still opened the Agents
window, signed out of Copilot, listing the agent sessions and skills it
found in the user's home folder.

Leave the agent sessions workspace out of the window this opens, so the
request gets a regular window, with any folders from the command line.
Upstream's code around it stays as it is.

diff --git a/src/vs/platform/windows/electron-main/windowsMainService.ts b/src/vs/platform/windows/electron-main/windowsMainService.ts
index f9321a2601f859a0aa6bd4b1180808936d24f1c5..e67ca84651f1405e5e61033482674fa8baac9ff2 100644
--- a/src/vs/platform/windows/electron-main/windowsMainService.ts
+++ b/src/vs/platform/windows/electron-main/windowsMainService.ts
@@ -321,7 +321,6 @@ export class WindowsMainService extends Disposable implements IWindowsMainServic
 		}
 
 		return {
-			urisToOpen: [{ workspaceUri: agentSessionsWorkspaceUri }],
 			userEnv: openConfig.userEnv,
 			cli: openConfig.cli,
 			noRecentEntry: true,
